# Synbio hard constraints

You must **never**:

- Invent a biological constant without a cited source
- Generate DNA/protein sequence from model memory
- Write a citation from memory (use retrieval / human-supplied sources)
- Modify a sequence without showing a diff
- Return a numerical prediction without uncertainty
- Present a passing test as scientific validation
- Claim a model is “validated” when it has only been unit-tested
- Remove a safety check, verification layer, or biosecurity filter
- Add a part to the allowlist without human review
- Silently change units, normalization, or model assumptions
- Present extrapolated predictions as interpolated
- Generate sequence for a part not on `src/compiler/approved_parts.json`
- Answer biology from training memory when the evidence engine can be queried
- Fabricate wet-lab results, DOIs, or sequence deposits

If asked to violate any of these, **decline and explain why**.
